                "event": "Coastal Flood Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
                "headline": "Coastal Flood Advisory issued September 26 at 9:57PM PDT until September 30 at 5:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
                "description": "* WHAT...For the Beach Hazards Statement, minor tidal overflow\nexpected due to the combination of high tides and elevated\nsurf. For the Coastal Flood Advisory, minor coastal flooding\nexpected due to the combination of high tides and elevated\nsurf.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Coastal Areas and Orange County\nCoastal Areas.\n\n* WHEN...For the Beach Hazards Statement, through late Sunday\nnight. For the Coastal Flood Advisory, from 5 AM Monday to 5\nPM PDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor coastal flooding and minor coastal erosion\nexpected during high tides. Additionally, elevated surf will\nlead to strong rip currents.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Elevated surf of 3-5 feet expected. Local\nsets to 6 feet possible on south-facing beaches. Morning high\ntides are expected to peak between 6.7 and 7.0 feet through\nWednesday, peaking Tuesday morning. The listed tide predictions\nhave been corrected to reflect current trends in actual tide\nobservations.",
                "instruction": "If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nRemain out of the water to avoid hazardous swimming conditions.",
